hey what is up guys I'm Kip EHD here  coming back at you from Las Vegas and  who would have thought the coolest booth  at CES 2015 would be a car company so  obviously there's tons of stuff at CES  that's really cool obviously to check  out and there are more videos on that  stuff to come but when you think of  hi-tech you rarely think of the ancient  hundred-year-old car industry and I've  talked about stuff that I guess Tesla's  done in the past year or so but BMW this  year had a legitimately awesome booth at  CES worth checking out so starting with  the BMW i8 totally dope looking car if  you couldn't already tell if you haven't  seen it I have some more stuff with that  coming up soon but if you don't already  know the i8 is one of the most badass  hybrid cars in the world with a  combination of an engine that has the  gas tank and an electric motor with  batteries that need to be charged now  I've showed off wireless charging of  phones in the past but leave it to BMW  to introduce inductive wireless charging  in their car so they're working on  basically driving up onto an inductive  wireless charging mat in your garage and  you're charging the battery at almost  the same rate as if you were physically  plugged in and here's another thing the  BMW m4 so this is their flagship sports  car right now essentially and they had a  showing with these concept lights on the  car oh LED tail lights and laser  headlights which seemed a little bit  weird but there are a ton of things that  this can become useful for the olla  taillights could theoretically be any  color you want and create any pattern or  any color and any frame rate which is  crazier basically using your tail lights  as a display on the back of your car but  they looked really sharp the only thing  I'd be hesitant about is if olee tail  lights would be bright enough obviously  they're doing this demo in a dark demo  showroom where everything's supposed to  be dark already but I would hope that  they're 